quran[9]{c,v,t}:
  32,12,"And if you could see when the guilty, hanging their heads (in shame) in the presence of their Lord, (will confess:) ‘Our Lord! We have seen and heard; therefore, send us back (to the world) so that we may act righteously. Indeed, we are (now) convinced.’"
  32,13,"And had We willed, We could have given each soul its guidance, but the Word from Me is confirmed (against the defiant): ‘I will indeed fill up Hell with the (guilty) jinn and humans all together.’"
  32,14,"So taste (the punishment), for you forgot the meeting of this day of yours. We (too) have forgotten you. And taste the everlasting punishment for what you used to do."
  32,15,"The (true) believers in Our revelations are only those who, when reminded of them, fall into prostration and glorify their Lord’s praise, and are not arrogant."
  32,16,"Their sides abandon their beds, calling upon their Lord out of fear and hope. And they spend (in charity) from what We have provided them."
  32,17,No soul knows what has been kept hidden for them of comfort to the eyes as a reward for what they used to do.
  32,18,Is one who believes like the one who is a transgressor? They are not equal.
  32,19,Those who believe and perform righteous deeds will have the Gardens of Eternal abode as a hospitality for what they used to do.
  32,20,"As for those who disobeyed, their refuge is the Fire. Whenever they desire to come out of it, they will be driven back into it and told: ‘Taste the torment of the Fire which you used to deny.’"
